{"created": "2025-10-01T17:38:08.305984+00:00", "modified": "2025-10-01T17:38:08.633874+00:00", "id": 17242926, "conceptrecid": "15107198", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17242926", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.15107198", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17242926", "metadata": {"title": "Systematic discovery of enzyme promiscuity in Escherichia coli using in vitro metabolomics: Preprocessed and normalized mass spectrometry data, Inputs & Outputs of computational pipeline", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.17242926", "publication_date": "2025-10-01", "description": "<p><span><a href=\"https://zenodo.org/api/records/17242926/draft/files/151210_FINAL_MAINdata_drift_log_iterativeZ_smooth_rp_fit_knowns_adducts.zip/content\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">151210_FINAL_MAINdata_drift_log_iterativeZ_smooth_rp_fit_knowns_adducts.zip</a></span> contains the datatables obtained after \"Spectral data processing and annotation\" and \"Data processing and standardization\" as described in Methods section.</p>\n<p>This repository also contains the datasets used as inputs for the computational pipeline to perform curvefitting and feature extraction on preprocessed MS data (=1= in&nbsp;<a href=\"https://zenodo.org/api/records/15116958/draft/files/MATLAB%3Dscripts1-3%3DINPUTSandOUTPUTS.7z/content\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MATLAB=scripts1-3=INPUTSandOUTPUTS.zip</a>), as well as outputs of this analysis and additional inputs required for machine learning approach (\"MachineLearning=INPUTS.7z\"), its output and additional inputs required for reconstructing full stoichiometries of promiscuous reactions based on identified changes in ion traces (=2= and =3= in <a href=\"https://zenodo.org/api/records/15116958/draft/files/MATLAB%3Dscripts1-3%3DINPUTSandOUTPUTS.7z/content\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MATLAB=scripts1-3=INPUTSandOUTPUTS.7z</a>).</p>", "access_right": "restricted", "creators": [{"name": "Gruber, Christoph Heinrich", "affiliation